# Deploy status after push

When you push to `main` or `master` (or the user asks you to push):

1. After a successful `git push`, do not stop at "pushed". Check the latest run of `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` for the pushed SHA.
2. Prefer `gh run list --workflow=deploy.yml --branch <branch> --limit 1` then `gh run watch <id>`. If `gh` is unavailable, fetch `https://api.github.com/repos/atri-konami/pcnk-counter/actions/workflows/deploy.yml/runs?per_page=5` and match `head_sha`.
3. Wait until the run completes (typically under a minute). Then report in Japanese: success or failure, the run URL, and the live site `https://atri-konami.github.io/pcnk-counter/`.
4. If it failed, summarize the failing step from the logs. If the run never appears, say so and link to [the workflow history](https://github.com/atri-konami/pcnk-counter/actions/workflows/deploy.yml).
